[{:db/id -1, :doc/id "doc-2605212020-session-post-mortem-2026-05-21", :doc/title "2026-05-21 session post-mortem — Tranche F closure governance + intentional code-port reverts", :doc/status "active", :doc/doc_type "explanation", :doc/source-format "edn", :doc/body "\n# 2026-05-21 session post-mortem\n\n**Date**: 2026-05-21 (evening JST)\n**Scope**: Tranche F closure (ADR-2605212100) Phase 3 + 4 + 5 + 6 governance + runbook layer + per-worker Python re-impl prototype attempts\n\n## What happened (chronological)\n\n1. **Opening question** (user): \"etzhayyim repo から etzhayyim への project の整理状況は?\"\n   — broad audit request on the org-split state.\n2. **Mid-session**: agent prototyped 27 per-worker SQLite ports + 4 ingest module ports + 4 substrate primitive ports in `etzhayyim/root/40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/src/kotodama/`,\n   following 6 patterns (BeliefStore / audit log / read-cache / primary store /\n   worker_runtime+stub / ingest module). Each port included a smoke test.\n3. **Reverts** (multiple system-reminder events): user intentionally reverted\n   the Python ports back to their pre-session vendor-RW state. The reverts\n   were systematic: substrate primitives + worker_main files + ingest modules\n   all returned to legacy state. Governance docs, runbooks, file relocates,\n   and vendor cross-references were KEPT.\n4. **Re-framing**: agent ran an honest disk audit, recognized the revert\n   pattern, and updated all surviving docs to say \"🟡 PATTERN ESTABLISHED,\n   EXECUTION OPEN\" for gate (a) instead of \"✅ CLOSED, 27/29 ported\".\n5. **Closure governance delivery**: 8 docs landed in this repo + 2 vendor-side\n   amendments. Phase 3+4+5+6 cutover is doc-runbook complete end-to-end.\n\n## What the reverts probably meant\n\nThe agent didn't get an explicit explanation, but the consistent pattern\nsuggests user intent:\n\n- **Keep**: governance docs (ADRs, surveys, runbooks, checklists),\n  cross-repo amendments (vendor `deps.toml` + vendor ADR-2605212100 §2\n  STATUS blocks), file-relocate operations (3 lg subtrees + 1 hume inline),\n  status snapshots, closure confirmations.\n- **Revert**: per-worker Python implementation code (the ~37 files in\n  `kotodama/` + 4 substrate primitives + 4 ingest modules).\n\nPossible reasons (agent's best guess; not confirmed):\n\n1. The per-worker ports may have had subtle bugs the agent didn't catch\n   in smoke tests (e.g. wrong column order, missing index, async/sync\n   confusion).\n2. The user may prefer to land per-worker ports as separate PRs with code\n   review rather than as session-internal bulk commits.\n3. The user may have a different implementation strategy in mind for some\n   workers and didn't want the agent's prototype to set precedent.\n4. The user may want the operational/governance work to land first (which\n   it did) and the code execution to happen in a more controlled context.\n\nIn any case, the **gate (a) execution checklist** (`90-docs/2605211949-...`)\nis the agent's contribution toward making future per-worker port attempts\nmore checkbox-trackable, regardless of who/when actually executes them.\n\n## Final disk state (post-revert, post-doc-sync)\n\n### etzhayyim/root\n\n**Survived**:\n\n- `README.edn` Status section update (+20 lines)\n- `90-docs/2605211800-vendor-importer-survey-gate-d.edn` (99 lines)\n- `90-docs/2605211900-tranche-f-all-gates-closure-confirmation.edn` (159 lines)\n- `90-docs/2605211949-gate-a-execution-checklist.edn` (200 lines)\n- `90-docs/2605212020-session-post-mortem-2026-05-21.edn` (this file)\n- `90-docs/TRANCHE-F-INDEX.edn` (120 lines)\n- `90-docs/adr/2605211757-dns-cutover-runbook-etzhayyim-ai-to-etzhayyim-com.edn` (431 lines)\n- `90-docs/adr/2605211913-vendor-refactor-and-git-rm-phase-4-5-runbook.edn` (388 lines)\n- `90-docs/adr/2605211925-phase-6-archive-markers-runbook.edn` (361 lines)\n- `60-apps/etzhayyim-project-curpus2skill/lg/` (7 files; gate (d) relocate)\n- `60-apps/etzhayyim-project-legal-entity/lg/` (7 files; gate (d) relocate)\n- (`60-apps/etzhayyim-project-ki/lg/lg_organism/` pre-existed before session)\n\n**Reverted**:\n\n- `40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/src/kotodama/primitives/active_inference_substrate.py`\n- `40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/src/kotodama/primitives/at_ipfs_belief_store.py`\n- `40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/src/kotodama/worker_runtime.py`\n- `40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/src/kotodama/ingest/core.py` (partially — still in\n  pre-port RW-dependent state)\n- 24 `*_worker_main.py` files in `kotodama/`\n- 3 `ingest/{blockchain,houbun,curpus2skill,site_common_crawl}.py` modules\n- An earlier-drafted standalone ADR-2605211653 (per-actor SQLite PVC); its\n  content was relocated inline to ADR-2605211757 §0 + §3.1\n\n### etzhayyim (etzhayyim-root)\n\n**Amended (uncommitted at session end)**:\n\n- `90-docs/adr/2605212100-kotodama-worker-3-axis-tranche-f-closure.edn` (+46 lines,\n  4 STATUS blocks + §2.5 cross-ref + status_note honest framing)\n- `deps.toml [[migrations]] etzhayyim-tranche-f-three-axis-split-2026-05-17`\n  (+10 lines, `gates_design_closed_at` + 2 operator-filled placeholder fields\n  + `closure_evidence` array)\n- `60-apps/etzhayyim-project-hume/scripts/_local_ingest_core.py` (193 lines, NEW;\n  gate (d) #4 inline copy of 4 ingest.core symbols with vendor RW write\n  semantics)\n- `60-apps/etzhayyim-project-hume/scripts/persist_hume_artifacts.py` (import\n  switch to `_local_ingest_core`)\n\n**Reverted** (or never modified):\n\n- All `kotodama/` worker / ingest / primitive files remain in their\n  pre-session state.\n\n## Cron loop state\n\nThe session has two cron tasks running:\n\n- `cc66dfbf` (active): `7,37 * * * *` → prompt `残りをすべて進めて`. Auto-expires\n  in 7 days. Session-only (dies when Claude session ends).\n- (`a54393cb` was cancelled mid-session when the user re-issued /loop with\n  the stronger \"進めて\" directive.)\n\n## Lessons for future sessions\n\n1. **The reverts are not noise**. When the user issues many small reverts in\n   a row, the right move is to (a) audit disk state, (b) update docs to match\n   that reality, (c) ask for clarification on which artifacts they want.\n2. **Governance work landed; code execution didn't**. This is a valid mid-state\n   — runbooks without execution are still useful (they make the next attempt\n   faster + more correct).\n3. **The gate (a) checklist** is the single most actionable artifact for the\n   next session/operator. 42 rows × ~15 minutes per row = ~10 hours of\n   focused per-worker port work + smoke tests.\n\n## What the next session should do\n\nIn rough priority order:\n\n1. **Confirm the user actually wants the per-worker ports** before re-attempting\n   them. If they do: work through the gate (a) checklist one row at a time,\n   pause for user review after each commit, never bulk-commit.\n2. **Or pivot**. The user may want to move past Tranche F entirely. Open items\n   in the etzhayyim/root README status table include:\n   - Bootstrap Council Seat 2-5 RFP (open until 2026-06-19)\n   - Base Sepolia testnet deploy (post-Council)\n   - The 220-file `etzhayyim` → `etzhayyim` cutover (blocked on 登記変更)\n3. **Or pure governance**. Add ADR amendments, update CLAUDE.md project-memory,\n   keep refining the Tranche F dossier — but be aware that the dossier has\n   passed the point of diminishing returns; further edits should be operator-\n   driven, not session-driven.\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2605212100 (Tranche F closure — gate definitions + classification table)\n- All session artifacts listed in `90-docs/TRANCHE-F-INDEX.edn`\n- etzhayyim-side `deps.toml [[migrations]] etzhayyim-tranche-f-three-axis-split-2026-05-17`\n  (cross-repo closure log target)\n", :doc/path "90-docs/2605212020-session-post-mortem-2026-05-21.edn", :doc/source-repo "root", :doc/topic "session-post-mortem-2026-05-21", :doc/last_verified "2026-05-21", :doc/date "2026-05-21", :doc/authoritative false, :doc/related ["adr-2605212100-kotodama-worker-3-axis-tranche-f-closure" "doc-2605211800-vendor-importer-survey-gate-d" "doc-2605211900-tranche-f-all-gates-closure-confirmation" "doc-2605211949-gate-a-execution-checklist"], :doc/authoritative_for ["2026-05-21 session intent + outcome" "explanation of why governance docs say 'PATTERN ESTABLISHED, EXECUTION OPEN' for gate (a)"]}]
